{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_8e76d82cf751abde3e08f3ab","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"kimi-k2.7-code","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. I implemented the benchmark run explorer in the four requested files and all tests pass.\n\n### What I built\n\n**`run-explorer.mjs`** — pure functions plus guarded browser code:\n- `filterRuns(runs, filters)`: validates the input array, applies `assistant`/`outcome` exact matches (with `all` disabling each filter), returns a new array.\n- `sortRuns(runs, order)`: supports `score-desc`, `time-asc`, and `cost-asc` with the specified tie-breakers; throws `TypeError` for bad inputs or unsupported orders.\n- `summarizeRuns(runs)`: returns `visibleCount`, `passRatePct` to one decimal, numeric median elapsed time, and a floating-point-safe `totalCostUsd` computed via whole cents.\n- Browser rendering is wrapped in `if (typeof document !== \"undefined\")` so the Node test runner can import the module safely.\n\n**`index.html`** — semantic layout with:\n- A main heading and note that these are sample records.\n- Labeled selects (`assistant-filter`, `outcome-filter`, `sort-order`) and a `Reset filters` button.\n- Summary values (`visible-count`, `pass-rate`, `median-time`, `known-cost`) with a note that subscription costs are excluded.\n- `aria-live=\"polite\"` status region, an initially `hidden` `empty-state`, and a `results-list` populated via safe DOM APIs (`createElement`, `textContent`).\n\n**`styles.css`** — responsive design with:\n- CSS custom properties for a clean visual hierarchy.\n- Desktop grid for results/summaries, switching to stacked layouts at `max-width: 720px`.\n- `:focus-visible` states, readable contrast, pass/fail outcome badges, and a `prefers-reduced-motion` rule.\n\n**`student-tests.mjs`** — three added edge-case tests:\n1. `sortRuns` `cost-asc` ordering: known costs first, then lower cost, then score/id ties, without mutating input.\n2. `summarizeRuns` empty-array behavior and even-length median averaging, plus input immutability.\n3. Type validation: non-array inputs and unsupported sort orders throw `TypeError`.\n\n### Test result\n\n```\n✔ filters by assistant and outcome without mutating the input\n✔ sorts score ties by faster elapsed time and then run ID\n✔ summarizes the visible runs\n✔ ships the required accessible, responsive interface hooks\n✔ sortRuns cost-asc places known costs first, ties on score and id\n✔ summarizeRuns handles empty arrays and even-length medians without mutation\n✔ filterRuns and sortRuns reject non-array inputs\nℹ tests 7\nℹ pass 7\nℹ fail 0\n```\n\n### Browser behavior I could not verify\nI only exercised the code through the Node test runner. I did not open the page in a browser, so I could not directly verify: actual select-change interactivity, the responsive breakpoint at 720 px, focus-visible outlines, hover card lift, reduced-motion behavior, or color-contrast rendering. The markup and styles are written to satisfy the contract and the regex-based test, but a real browser pass would be needed to confirm the full UX."}],"usage":{"input_tokens":16140,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1020fe11-6e6c-4920-9e00-77795660475d","uuid":"285e2168-cde3-4586-b4d7-488f6b198596","timestamp":"2026-08-23T14:32:02.206Z"}
